.TH MSGRAPH-SENDMAIL 1 "July 2026" "msgraph-sendmail 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
msgraph-sendmail \- send mail through the Microsoft Graph API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B msgraph-sendmail
[\fB\-t\fR] [\fB\-i\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fIfrom\fR] [\fIsendmail options\fR...] [\fIrecipient\fR...]
.br
.B msgraph-sendmail
\fB\-bv\fR \fIrecipient\fR...
.br
.B msgraph-sendmail
\fB\-\-to\fR \fIaddr\fR [\fB\-\-subject\fR \fItext\fR] [\fB\-\-body\fR \fItext\fR] [\fIoptions\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B msgraph-sendmail
is a drop-in replacement for the classic
.BR sendmail (8)
binary that submits mail to Microsoft Exchange Online through the
Microsoft Graph API over HTTPS, using an Entra ID app registration with
the
.B Mail.Send
application permission (OAuth 2.0 client credentials flow).
.PP
In the default
.I sendmail mode
it reads an RFC 822/MIME message from standard input. In
.I CLI mode
(activated by any long message option such as \fB\-\-to\fR) it builds the
message from command-line arguments.
.SH SENDMAIL MODE OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-t
Read recipients from the To:, Cc: and Bcc: headers. Bcc recipients are
honoured but not disclosed.
.TP
.BI \-f " address" ", \-r " address
Set the sender mailbox. Overrides the From: header and the configured
default.
.TP
.B \-i, \-oi
Do not treat a line consisting of a single dot as end of input.
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose output on standard error.
.TP
.B \-bv
Verify addresses: print how each recipient resolves (see
.BR "LOCAL ADDRESSES" )
and exit without reading stdin or sending anything. Exit status 67 if any
address cannot be resolved. Also accepted as \fB\-b v\fR.
.TP
.B \-bi, \-bp, \-bm
\fB\-bi\fR (newaliases) does nothing, as aliases are read live;
\fB\-bp\fR (mailq) reports an empty queue; \fB\-bm\fR is the default.
Other modes, such as \fB\-bs\fR (SMTP on stdin), are rejected with exit
status 64.
.PP
All other traditional sendmail options are accepted and ignored for
compatibility.
.SH CLI MODE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-to " addr"
Add recipient(s); repeatable, accepts comma-separated lists.
.TP
.BI \-\-cc " addr" ", \-\-bcc " addr ", \-\-reply\-to " addr
Add Cc/Bcc/Reply-To recipients.
.TP
.BI \-\-subject " text"
Message subject.
.TP
.BI \-\-body " text" ", \-\-body\-file " file
Message body. When neither is given, the body is read from stdin.
.TP
.B \-\-html
Treat the body as HTML.
.TP
.BI \-\-attach " file"
Attach a file; repeatable.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-from " addr"
Sender mailbox.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Use an alternate configuration file.
.TP
.B \-\-save\-to\-sent, \-\-no\-save\-to\-sent
Keep (or don't keep) a copy in the sender's Sent Items folder.
Default: keep.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-time " seconds"
Time budget for the whole run, including retries and pauses (default 50,
0 = no limit). Overrides
.BR max_time .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the Graph API payload instead of sending.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-\-version, \-\-help
The usual.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Read from the first of:
.BR \-\-config ,
.BR $MSGRAPH_SENDMAIL_CONFIG ,
.IR ~/.config/msgraph\-sendmail.conf ,
.IR /etc/msgraph\-sendmail.conf .
INI format, section [msgraph], keys:
.BR tenant ,
.BR client_id ,
.BR client_secret ,
.BR client_secret_file ,
.BR from ,
.BR save_to_sent ,
.BR timeout ,
.BR max_time ,
.BR local_recipient ,
.BR aliases_file ,
.BR local_domains ;
optional section [aliases].
Environment variables
.B MSGRAPH_SENDMAIL_TENANT
etc. override the file. The file contains a secret; keep it mode 600.
.SH LOCAL ADDRESSES
An address is
.I local
when it has no domain (\fBroot\fR) or its domain is in
.B local_domains
(default: localhost, localhost.localdomain, the host name and FQDN, but
never the domain of the configured
.BR from ).
Local recipients are resolved through the [aliases] section of the
configuration, then the aliases file (default
.IR /etc/aliases ,
recursively; pipe, file and :include: targets are skipped), and finally
the
.B local_recipient
catch-all; /dev/null discards. A local recipient that resolves to
nothing makes the whole message fail with exit status 67. The aliases
file must be a regular file owned by root (or the caller) and not
writable by group or others. Local sender addresses (\fB\-f\fR, From:)
are skipped when choosing the sending mailbox, so cron and daemon mail is
sent from the configured
.BR from .
.SH TIME LIMITS AND RETRIES
Each network operation is limited by
.B timeout
(default 15 s) and the whole run by
.B max_time
(default 50 s). Network errors, HTTP 429 and 5xx are retried up to 4
times with pauses of 2, 4 and 8 s, honouring a Retry-After of at most
30 s, but never beyond
.BR max_time .
A retry after the request may already have reached Graph can deliver the
message twice; this is logged. When the budget runs out, or on SIGTERM,
SIGHUP, SIGINT or SIGALRM, the tool logs the stage and elapsed time to
syslog and exits 75.
.SH EXIT STATUS
BSD sysexits: 0 success, 64 usage error, 65 bad message, 67 unknown
local address, 69 service
refused (auth/permissions), 75 temporary failure, time budget exhausted or
aborted by a signal (retry), 78
configuration error.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/msgraph\-sendmail.conf
.br
.I ~/.config/msgraph\-sendmail.conf
.br
.I /etc/aliases
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sendmail (8),
.BR aliases (5)
.PP
Full documentation:
.I https://github.com/maciejczub/msgraph\-sendmail
